      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🧠 Controller Agent – Multi-Agent Workflow Pattern\n\nThe **Controller Agent** is like the “manager” in a multi-agent system. Instead of doing the task itself, the controller inspects the user’s input or problem and decides **which specialized agent** should handle it.\n\nThink of it like a smart traffic director:  \nIt doesn’t write content or answer questions directly — it just **routes the task** to the best agent for the job.\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 The Intuition Behind Controller Agents\n\nImagine calling a customer service line:\n- You press 1 for sales  \n- Press 2 for support  \n- Press 3 for billing\n\nThe system doesn’t solve your problem — it **routes you to the right expert**.\n\nThat’s exactly what a Controller Agent does in an n8n AI workflow.\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ How It Works in n8n\n\n1. A user question or task is received.\n2. A **Switch node** or **OpenAI-based router agent** checks the intent.\n3. Based on conditions (like keywords or classification), it routes the input to:\n   - A writing agent\n   - A math solver\n   - A product recommender\n   - A code generator\n   - ...or any other specialized agent.\n\nYou’re essentially building a **logic-based decision tree** with intelligent routing.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Real-Life Example\n\nSuppose the input is:\n> “What is the capital of France?”\n\nThe controller sees the word **“capital”** and routes the task to a **Geography Agent**.\n\nAnother input:\n> “What’s 12% of 240?”\n\nIt matches **math keywords**, so the controller sends it to the **Math Solver Agent**.\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 Dynamic Controller with LLM\n\nYou can even make your controller an **AI-powered router** by asking OpenAI to:\n> “Classify this task into categories: Writing, Math, Code, or Other”\n\nThen use the output to control the flow dynamically.\n\n---\n\n### 💡 When to Use Controller Agents\n\n- When your users may send **different types of questions**\n- When you want **multiple tools or agents to coexist**\n- When you want to keep your workflow **organized and expandable**\n\nIt’s especially useful in chatbots, form handlers, or knowledge assistants.\n\n---\n\n### 🔗 Connect with Me\n\nWant to learn how to build controller-agent logic in n8n using LLMs and conditions?\n\n📺 **YouTube** → [@tech.mayankagg](https://www.youtube.com/@tech.mayankagg)  \n💼 **LinkedIn** → [Mayank Agarwal](https://www.linkedin.com/in/mayank953/)  \n📸 **Instagram** → [@tech.mayankagg](https://www.instagram.com/tech.mayankagg/)\n\n---\n\n*Shared by Mayank Agarwal – Teaching AI workflows that actually scale.*\n",
